Three checks that were not checking the measured run, and the telemetry field no
report ever carried -- trn1.2xlarge, 2026-09-12 (UTC).

1. kv_cache_churn's landing check. It read one cache element and failed only if
   that element still held CACHE_FILL. The loop that compiles each ring slot
   writes every slot first, so the element held ENTRY_FILL before the clock
   started: the check passed whatever the timed loop did. The cache is now put
   back to CACHE_FILL after the slots compile, and every slot the loop should
   have written is read afterwards, in both caches.

2. transformer_train_step sampled its parameter before the warm-up, which is a
   full forward/backward/optimiser step, so "the model moved" could be
   satisfied by an update nobody measured. It is now sampled after the warm-up.

3. neuron_monitor read memory_used.neuron_runtime_used_bytes.device. Hardware
   writes neuron_device (data/probe-2026-08-26/07-neuron-monitor-schema.txt),
   so device_memory_used_bytes was absent from every report the suite has
   written -- and the schema test's fixture carried the probe's own number
   under the parser's key, so it passed.

